{"audit_run_id":"audit:e81b8e800d3748539305c787193658f4","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":92,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"The data file is `ostrich_chick_grower_trial.csv`. One row is one ostrich chick. Sixty-four"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"individually identified chicks were reared on a commercial farm to 90 days of age, 32 on the"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"farm's standard grower ration and 32 on the lucerne-enriched, higher-fibre grower ration. Each"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"chick was measured once at the end of the rearing period, so the file holds 64 data rows plus a"},{"end_column":64,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"header row and every chick has a value in every outcome column."},{"end_column":28,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"| Column | Meaning | Unit |"},{"end_column":28,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"|--------|---------|------|"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"| `bird_id` | Identifier of the individual chick, `OS001` through `OS064` | none (identifier) |"},{"end_column":114,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"| `diet_group` | Rearing diet the chick was allocated to: `standard` or `lucerne_enriched` | none (group label) |"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"| `body_weight_kg` | Live body weight at 90 days of age | kilograms (kg) |"},{"end_column":116,"end_line":16,"start_column":1,"start_line":16,"text":"| `average_daily_gain_g_per_day` | Average daily live-weight gain over the rearing period | grams per day (g/day) |"},{"end_column":127,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"| `feed_conversion_ratio` | Feed consumed per unit of live-weight gain; lower is more efficient | none (kg feed per kg gain) |"},{"end_column":112,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"| `tibiotarsus_length_cm` | Length of the tibiotarsus, the main lower leg bone, at 90 days | centimetres (cm) |"},{"end_column":92,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"| `hock_circumference_cm` | Circumference of the hock joint at 90 days | centimetres (cm) |"},{"end_column":103,"end_line":20,"start_column":1,"start_line":20,"text":"| `serum_total_protein_g_per_l` | Total protein concentration in blood serum | grams per litre (g/L) |"},{"end_column":102,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| `serum_calcium_mmol_per_l` | Calcium concentration in blood serum | millimoles per litre (mmol/L) |"},{"end_column":116,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| `packed_cell_volume_percent` | Packed cell volume, the share of blood volume made up of red cells | percent (%) |"},{"end_column":86,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"The measurements are invented for this project rather than collected from real birds."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"`analysis.py` reads the CSV and compares the two diets on each of the eight outcomes declared in"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"the trial protocol, in the declared order. Every outcome is tested the same way, with a two-sided"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"two-sample Welch t-test, and the verdict for each outcome is read at the conventional 0.05"},{"end_column":91,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"threshold. Group sizes are 32 standard and 32 lucerne-enriched for all eight outcomes. The"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"difference reported below is the lucerne-enriched mean minus the standard mean."},{"end_column":89,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"Standard 48.7406, lucerne-enriched 46.7687, difference -1.9719. t = -2.8719, p = 0.0056."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"Significant at 0.05. Chicks on the lucerne-enriched ration were about 2 kg lighter at the end of"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"rearing. On a slaughter-weight basis that is a real loss of saleable body mass per bird, and it"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"would either shave the carcass weight at a fixed age or push back the age at which target weight"},{"end_column":12,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"is reached."},{"end_column":92,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"Standard 481.6250, lucerne-enriched 462.0000, difference -19.6250. t = -3.6047, p = 0.0007."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":49,"start_column":1,"start_line":49,"text":"Significant at 0.05. Growth was about 20 g/day slower on the lucerne-enriched ration, which is"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":50,"start_column":1,"start_line":50,"text":"the same story as the body weight result seen as a rate. Sustained over a rearing period this is"},{"end_column":39,"end_line":51,"start_column":1,"start_line":51,"text":"what produces the lighter final birds."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"Standard 3.1525, lucerne-enriched 3.3937, difference 0.2412. t = 5.5527, p = 0.0000 (below"},{"end_column":9,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"0.0001)."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":58,"start_column":1,"start_line":58,"text":"Significant at 0.05. Birds on the lucerne-enriched ration needed about 0.24 kg more feed for each"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"kilogram of gain, so they were less efficient. Feed is the dominant cost in growing ostriches, and"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":60,"start_column":1,"start_line":60,"text":"a gap this size raises the feed bill per kilogram produced. This is the most clear-cut difference"},{"end_column":14,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"in the trial."},{"end_column":87,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"Standard 38.2594, lucerne-enriched 38.2781, difference 0.0187. t = 0.0622, p = 0.9506."},{"end_column":92,"end_line":67,"start_column":1,"start_line":67,"text":"Not significant at 0.05. Long-bone growth was effectively identical on the two rations. The"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"higher-fibre diet did not hold back skeletal length, which matters because stunted leg growth in"},{"end_column":55,"end_line":69,"start_column":1,"start_line":69,"text":"fast-growing ratites is associated with leg disorders."},{"end_column":87,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"Standard 12.8844, lucerne-enriched 13.3156, difference 0.4313. t = 3.2208, p = 0.0021."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"Significant at 0.05. Hocks were about 0.43 cm thicker on the lucerne-enriched ration. A thicker"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":76,"start_column":1,"start_line":76,"text":"hock joint alongside unchanged bone length is consistent with a slightly sturdier leg conformation"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":77,"start_column":1,"start_line":77,"text":"rather than with the classic mismatch of heavy body on slender legs. It should still be watched,"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":78,"start_column":1,"start_line":78,"text":"because hock swelling can also be a sign of joint problems, and this measurement alone cannot tell"},{"end_column":29,"end_line":79,"start_column":1,"start_line":79,"text":"sturdier apart from swollen."},{"end_column":87,"end_line":83,"start_column":1,"start_line":83,"text":"Standard 35.4844, lucerne-enriched 36.2750, difference 0.7906. t = 1.7412, p = 0.0866."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":85,"start_column":1,"start_line":85,"text":"Not significant at 0.05. Protein status in blood looked the same on both rations. Both group means"},{"end_column":90,"end_line":86,"start_column":1,"start_line":86,"text":"sit inside the range expected for healthy growing ostriches, so there is no sign that the"},{"end_column":51,"end_line":87,"start_column":1,"start_line":87,"text":"higher-fibre ration compromised protein nutrition."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":91,"start_column":1,"start_line":91,"text":"Standard 2.3684, lucerne-enriched 2.4569, difference 0.0884. t = 3.8780, p = 0.0003."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":93,"start_column":1,"start_line":93,"text":"Significant at 0.05. Serum calcium was about 0.09 mmol/L higher on the lucerne-enriched ration,"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":94,"start_column":1,"start_line":94,"text":"which fits lucerne being a calcium-rich forage. Both means remain within the normal range, so this"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":95,"start_column":1,"start_line":95,"text":"reads as a mild dietary shift in mineral supply rather than a disorder. It is worth keeping in view"},{"end_column":98,"end_line":96,"start_column":1,"start_line":96,"text":"when setting the calcium and phosphorus balance of the ration, since an oversupply of calcium can"},{"end_column":52,"end_line":97,"start_column":1,"start_line":97,"text":"interfere with phosphorus and trace mineral uptake."},{"end_column":87,"end_line":101,"start_column":1,"start_line":101,"text":"Standard 30.1250, lucerne-enriched 30.4563, difference 0.3313. t = 0.9816, p = 0.3302."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":103,"start_column":1,"start_line":103,"text":"Not significant at 0.05. Red cell volume was comparable on both rations and both means fall in the"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":104,"start_column":1,"start_line":104,"text":"normal range for growing ostriches, giving no indication of anaemia or dehydration on either diet."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":108,"start_column":1,"start_line":108,"text":"Five of the eight declared outcomes differed significantly at the 0.05 threshold: body weight,"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":109,"start_column":1,"start_line":109,"text":"average daily gain, feed conversion ratio, hock circumference and serum calcium. Tibiotarsus"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":110,"start_column":1,"start_line":110,"text":"length, serum total protein and packed cell volume did not differ."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":112,"start_column":1,"start_line":112,"text":"The pattern splits cleanly. On production, the lucerne-enriched ration was worse on all three"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":113,"start_column":1,"start_line":113,"text":"measures: lighter birds, slower gain, and more feed needed per kilogram of gain. On health and"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":114,"start_column":1,"start_line":114,"text":"skeletal development, it was neutral to mildly favourable: bone length, blood protein and packed"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":115,"start_column":1,"start_line":115,"text":"cell volume were unchanged, hock circumference was slightly larger, and serum calcium was slightly"},{"end_column":42,"end_line":116,"start_column":1,"start_line":116,"text":"higher while staying in the normal range."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":120,"start_column":1,"start_line":120,"text":"Keep the standard grower ration as the default for chicks reared to 90 days. The lucerne-enriched"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":121,"start_column":1,"start_line":121,"text":"ration cost roughly 2 kg of body weight and 0.24 kg of feed per kilogram of gain without buying any"},{"end_column":37,"end_line":122,"start_column":1,"start_line":122,"text":"measured health advantage in return."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":124,"start_column":1,"start_line":124,"text":"Lucerne need not be abandoned outright. Two narrower uses are worth testing before any change to"},{"end_column":24,"end_line":125,"start_column":1,"start_line":125,"text":"the standard programme:"},{"end_column":93,"end_line":127,"start_column":1,"start_line":127,"text":"1. A lower lucerne inclusion rate, aimed at keeping the calcium and fibre contribution while"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":128,"start_column":4,"start_line":128,"text":"recovering most of the growth and efficiency lost at the rate used here."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":129,"start_column":1,"start_line":129,"text":"2. Lucerne later in the growing period, once the fastest growth phase is past and cheaper bulk feed"},{"end_column":23,"end_line":130,"start_column":4,"start_line":130,"text":"is more attractive."},{"end_column":91,"end_line":132,"start_column":1,"start_line":132,"text":"Whichever is tried, record hock condition alongside circumference. The larger hocks on the"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":133,"start_column":1,"start_line":133,"text":"lucerne-enriched ration are compatible with sturdier joints and with early joint swelling, and this"},{"end_column":96,"end_line":134,"start_column":1,"start_line":134,"text":"trial cannot separate the two. A follow-up trial should also confirm the calcium and phosphorus"},{"end_column":74,"end_line":135,"start_column":1,"start_line":135,"text":"balance of any lucerne-containing ration before it goes into routine use."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:fd57a4b40d834763b3cb","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:79d41821f712aa2bd99830d186947544df7278426e59003d811e86666aa34bf1","end_line":135,"locator":"report.md:1-135","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
